-- title:
--   Negation is a variable change fixing every Weierstrass curve
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$, i.e. a tuple of coefficients $a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4, a_6 \in R$ presenting $y^2 + a_1xy + a_3y = x^3 + a_2x^2 + a_4x + a_6$. Consider the element of the variable-change group `VariableChange R` whose data are the unit $u = -1$ of $R$ and the ring elements $r = 0$, $s = -W.a_1$, $t = -W.a_3$; this is the substitution $(x,y) \mapsto (x, -y - a_1x - a_3)$ in Mathlib's normalisation. The theorem asserts that the action of this element on $W$ returns $W$ itself, as an equality of Weierstrass curves over $R$, that is, all five transformed coefficients $u^{-1}(a_1 + 2s)$, $u^{-2}(a_2 - sa_1 + 3r - s^2)$, $u^{-3}(a_3 + ra_1 + 2t)$, $u^{-4}(a_4 - sa_3 + 2ra_2 - (t + rs)a_1 + 3r^2 - 2st)$ and $u^{-6}(a_6 + ra_4 + r^2a_2 + r^3 - ta_3 - t^2 - rta_1)$ coincide with $a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4, a_6$ respectively for this choice of $(u, r, s, t)$. No hypothesis beyond commutativity of $R$ is required.
--
--   This records the group-law negation $P \mapsto -P$ as an element of the variable-change group $\{(u,r,s,t)\}$ which stabilises every Weierstrass curve, so that the stabiliser of a curve under the variable-change action always contains the two-element subgroup generated by it. It is used in counting arguments about orbits and stabilisers of the variable-change action, in [`WeierstrassCurve.natCard_fibre_dvd_jWidth_of_variableChange_orbitMap`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.natCard_fibre_dvd_jWidth_of_variableChange_orbitMap) and in [`ModularCurve.ord_jGeomGen_sub_algebraMap_eq_one_of_evalAt_eq_of_le_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_jGeomGen_sub_algebraMap_eq_one_of_evalAt_eq_of_le_three).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_variableChange_mk_neg_one_smul_eq_self.lean

